From: Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] components/private_verification_tokens: reach ATHM through a cxx bridge, not Crubit

Upstream 4ff7d01fb98f ("[PVT] Migrate athm_ffi to use Crubit instead of
cxx", 2026-08-19) moved the ATHM bindings from a `cxx` bridge to a Crubit
`cpp_api_from_rust` binding, and every later M154 commit on the component
(735803eb7770, b329dcd5811f, 0aa0cdb45b46, 3f46f9bfb3ad, ...) builds on
it.  `cpp_api_from_rust` only exists when `enable_cpp_api_from_rust` is
true, and //build/config/rust.gni turns it false whenever
`rust_sysroot_absolute` is set, so with a system Rust sysroot gn never
defines `athm_ffi_bindings` and `gn gen` dies:

  ERROR Unresolved dependencies.
  //components/private_verification_tokens/common:privacy_pass_athm_batch_request(...)
    needs //components/private_verification_tokens/common/athm_ffi:athm_ffi_bindings(...)

Unlike components/web_package (chromium-154-revert-signed-web-bundles-
crubit.patch) this cannot be a revert: //chrome/browser/
private_verification_tokens already consumes the M154 API, and the
commits stacked on top of the migration would have to go too.  So the
Rust crate is kept exactly as upstream ships it, and only the binding
layer is swapped:

 - athm_ffi/athm_cxx.rs (new) is a `cxx` bridge over the five client
   operations PrivacyPassAthmBatchRequest calls.  `cxx` cannot return a
   `Result` without C++ exceptions, so a failed constructor yields an
   object whose `*_ok()` accessor is false, and `finalize` returns bool
   with an out-parameter.
 - privacy_pass_athm_batch_request.{h,cc} hold `rust::Box`es of the
   bridge types instead of the Crubit ones, and pass slices through
   base::SpanToRustSlice as they did in M153.  Behaviour is unchanged.
 - AthmTestIssuer drives the *issuer* half through Crubit.  It is
   test-only, so it and the two unit tests built on it are gated on
   `enable_cpp_api_from_rust` rather than ported.  The chrome/browser
   test targets list it as a dependency but no source there includes it.

Same reachability as chromium-153-revert-font-format-crubit.patch:
applied only with USE=-bundled-toolchain.  Drop this patch once the
overlay builds Crubit for the system toolchain, or upstream gates the
dependency on `enable_cpp_api_from_rust`.
